== 2026-11-20 07:08:07 #1025 lane S: the D 13, k_c 31 control misread ('mixed', lane_s.log 07:00); the stop rule held the D 17 track. Cause, from svddiag.py (07:04-07:05, run while lane S's refine ran: a third process for 76 s, the pause hit its timeout wrapper):
  The V is regular: sigma/sigma_max of lambda_1's triplet 7.81e-08 (+0.03), 2.49e-08 (+0.01), 6.89e-09 (+0.003), 2.73e-09 (+0.001); 5.71e-15 at lam1.
  On its way down it crosses regular singular pairs (1.20e-08/1.22e-08 and 1.40e-08/1.41e-08 between +0.01 and +0.003; 2.05e-09/2.06e-09
  between +0.003 and +0.001). At each crossing its right vector mixes with the partner:
    0.01->0.003: top overlaps 0.881 @ 6.89e-09, 0.470 @ 1.26e-08 (sum of squares 0.997)
    0.003->0.001: top overlaps 0.869 @ 2.73e-09, 0.481 @ 1.75e-09
  The 0.9 overlap rule breaks the chain there. The planted test had no regular values along the V's path, so it never met a crossing.
Planted crossing case (svdtrack.py planted, a V with slope 2.5e-6 coupled to six regular values as at D 13; couplings chosen to give D 13's
mixing): with the 0.9 rule 'mixed' (reproduces the control); with --track=majority (overlap^2 >= 0.5) the chain holds and the pair joins
(overlap 0.927), but the fitted roots are 1.999897 (outer) and 2.000450 (inner) against 2.0: off by -1.0e-4 and +4.5e-4, so 'mixed' again.
Level repulsion at the crossings bends sigma, so a fit of sigma at offsets 0.003-0.03 is biased by ~1e-4 to 5e-4 even for a genuine V.
No criterion was changed and the D 17 track was not run.
